# Shared .dockerignore for HDS Node backend services (plan 102), from
# `infra/dev-deploy/templates/dockerignore`.
#
# Two jobs. First, keep the build context small and the image reproducible. Second,
# and more important: make sure a developer's gitignored credential files can never
# be swept into a build context. CI builds from a clean checkout so they are not
# present there, but `docker build` run by hand on a working tree would pick them up.
# Patterns use `**/` so they also match inside nested packages.

# --- credentials and local config: never in an image ---
**/localConfig*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/backloop.dev.json
**/secrets/
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- build output / installed deps (the image installs and builds its own) ---
**/node_modules
dist
coverage

# --- runtime state that must come from the Dokku storage mount, not the image ---
storage/
data/
debugLog/
**/application.log
**/*.log

# --- repo furniture with no runtime role ---
# (hds-mcp-js keeps tsconfig*.json: the image runs `npm run build`.)
.git
.github
.gitignore
tests
test
doc
docs
_notes
*.md
!README.md
eslint.config.*
.editorconfig
